preventionRule:
Wrap every fetch() to a local engine endpoint with a timeout signal:
  const ctrl = new AbortController();
  const tid = setTimeout(() => ctrl.abort(), 8000);
  try {
    const resp = await fetch(url, { signal: ctrl.signal });
    // ...
  } catch (e) {
    if (e.name === 'AbortError') { /* timeout */ }
    else throw e;
  } finally {
    clearTimeout(tid);
  }
Or use AbortSignal.timeout(8000) if targeting modern browsers only.
